      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;tufte-style-features&#34;&gt;Tufte-Style Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm implements several features inspired by Edward Tufte&amp;rsquo;s typographic principles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;margin-notes&#34;&gt;Margin Notes&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;marginnote&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for margin notes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;input id=&#34;marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;marginpar-ctrl&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;&lt;label for=&#34;marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;has-counter&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;span id=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;marginpar &#34; role=&#34;note&#34;&gt;This note appears in the margin.&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;margin-par&#34;&gt;Margin Par&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;marginpar&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for margin paragraphs:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;input id=&#34;marginpar-1&#34; class=&#34;marginpar-ctrl&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;&lt;label for=&#34;marginpar-1&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;span id=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34; class=&#34;marginpar &#34; role=&#34;note&#34;&gt;This is a margin paragraph with more detailed content.&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;epigraphs&#34;&gt;Epigraphs&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;epigraph&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for epigraphs:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div role=&#34;doc-epigraph&#34; class=&#34;epigraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;    The best way to predict the future is to invent it.&#xA;— Alan Kay&#xA;    &lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;theorem&#34;&gt;Theorem&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;theorem&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for mathematical theorems:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <content:encoded>&lt;h2 id=&#34;tufte-style-features&#34;&gt;Tufte-Style Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm implements several features inspired by Edward Tufte&amp;rsquo;s typographic principles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;margin-notes&#34;&gt;Margin Notes&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;marginnote&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for margin notes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;input id=&#34;marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;marginpar-ctrl&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;&lt;label for=&#34;marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;has-counter&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;span id=&#34;the-marginnote-0&#34; class=&#34;marginpar &#34; role=&#34;note&#34;&gt;This note appears in the margin.&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;margin-par&#34;&gt;Margin Par&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;marginpar&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for margin paragraphs:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;input id=&#34;marginpar-1&#34; class=&#34;marginpar-ctrl&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;&lt;label for=&#34;marginpar-1&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; aria-label=&#34;Additional Notes&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;&lt;span id=&#34;the-marginpar-1&#34; class=&#34;marginpar &#34; role=&#34;note&#34;&gt;This is a margin paragraph with more detailed content.&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;epigraphs&#34;&gt;Epigraphs&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;epigraph&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for epigraphs:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div role=&#34;doc-epigraph&#34; class=&#34;epigraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;    The best way to predict the future is to invent it.&#xA;— Alan Kay&#xA;    &lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;theorem&#34;&gt;Theorem&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;theorem&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for mathematical theorems:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;span role=&#34;presentation&#34; id=&#34;pythagorean-theorem&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;style&gt;&#xA;    #pythagorean-theorem {&#xA;        counter-reset: pythagorean-theorem;&#xA;    }&#xA;    .pythagorean-theorem::after {&#xA;        counter-increment: pythagorean-theorem;&#xA;        content: &#39; &#39; counter(pythagorean-theorem) &#39;. &#39;;&#xA;    }&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote role=&#34;complementary&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;pythagorean-theorem textssc&#34; role=&#34;heading&#34;&gt;Pythagorean Theorem&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    In a right triangle, a² + b² = c².&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;figure&#34;&gt;Figure&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use the &lt;code&gt;figure&lt;/code&gt; shortcode for figures with captions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-html&#34; data-lang=&#34;html&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure &gt;&#xA;    &lt;input id=&#34;fig-8d8f0be5b35c3233b13a6626f015e624-4&#34; class=&#34;marginpar-ctrl&#34; type=&#34;checkbox&#34; aria-controls=&#34;the-fig-8d8f0be5b35c3233b13a6626f015e624-4&#34; hidden&gt;&#xA;    &lt;label for=&#34;fig-8d8f0be5b35c3233b13a6626f015e624-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;        &lt;span id=&#34;the-fig-8d8f0be5b35c3233b13a6626f015e624-4&#34; class=&#34;marginpar abs&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    Figure 1: A sample diagram&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/img/diagram.png&#34;aria-describedby=&#34;fig-8d8f0be5b35c3233b13a6626f015e624-4&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            &gt;&#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</content:encoded>
